@voiceinsideyou next try... with this I can no longer see the CPU spinning. 

https://oss.sonatype.org/content/repositories/snapshots/io/netty/netty/3.6.5.Final-SNAPSHOT/netty-3.6.5.Final-20130408.083213-9.jar

Please give a spin (but no cpu spin ;))

Functionally looks better now - thanks! Minor nitpick with the overflow error message:

```
    // Convert tickDuration to nanos.
    this.tickDuration = tickDuration = unit.toNanos(tickDuration);

    // Prevent overflow.
    if (tickDuration == Long.MAX_VALUE ||
            tickDuration >= Long.MAX_VALUE / wheel.length) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                "tickDuration is too long: " +
                tickDuration +  ' ' + unit);
    }
```

if I give a duration in, say, seconds the error message above will display "tickDuration is too long: durationInNanos seconds" which is a bit misleading; since the tickDuration parameter value is rewritten in the conversion. Possibly should just not change the value of the parameter in the assignment and then compare this.tickDuration for overflow, while retaining the error message being printed alongside whatever units the caller specified?
